course: dictionary
lesson: 8848
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it and ask: what would fit here? «Humpback whales blow a spiral net of bubbles that traps a shoal of fish.» Fish are swimming near each other, so a shoal must be a large group of fish.
explain: «The ship ran aground on a shoal near the coast.» A ship cannot run into a group of fish. Ran aground and near the coast are the clues, so here a shoal is a shallow sandbank that can be dangerous for boats.
explain: Sometimes a word is used in an everyday, informal way. «We got shoals of letters this morning.» Letters are not swimming in a group, so shoals here means a large number of them. Try your meaning in the sentence: a lot of letters makes sense.
fact: A shoal is a large group of fish swimming together.
fact: Fish often shoal for safety: it is harder for a predator to pick out one fish, and many eyes spot danger.
fact: A shoal can also be a shallow place in a sea or river, often a sandbank, that can be dangerous for boats.
fact: Lighthouses warn ships about shoals near coasts.
fact: Informally, shoals of things means a large number of them, as in «shoals of letters».
exercise: «Humpback whales work together to trap a shoal of fish.» What is a shoal here? | A small lighthouse | A shallow sandbank | *A large group of fish swimming together | A kind of whale
exercise: «The ship ran aground on a shoal near the coast.» What is a shoal here? | A type of wave | *A shallow sandbank that can be dangerous for boats | A net of bubbles | A group of fish
exercise: Mia says, «We got shoals of letters this morning.» What does shoals mean? | Shallow water near the beach | *A large number of letters | Boats in the harbour | Small fish
test: In «most are timid scavengers that shoal for safety», what does shoal mean? | To run aground | To blow bubbles | *To swim in a large group | To bite
test: Why do fish swim in a shoal? | *For safety, because many eyes spot danger and a predator finds it harder to pick out one fish | To build nests on the sea floor | To hide from the sun | To make bubbles
exam: Which of these is a meaning of shoal? | A small boat used for fishing | A piece of seaweed | *A shallow sandbank that can be dangerous for boats | A tall tower with a light to warn ships
